IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgh-incorporation`

-- Tests for sgh-incorporation.l4 (ss 19, 20 and 20A). Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion, before the run.

§ `s 19: registration and incorporation`
-- (test alias a19a = `s 19(1) the person desiring the incorporation of the company has done everything the subsection requires`)
-- arguments: submitted the constitution and documents; furnished the last day of the first financial year and information; paid the prescribed fee
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the person desiring the incorporation of the company has done everything the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) submit ...; (b) furnish ...; and (c) pay the Registrar the prescribed fee": all three
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the person desiring the incorporation of the company has done everything the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) unmet
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the person desiring the incorporation of the company has done everything the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) unmet
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the person desiring the incorporation of the company has done everything the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c) unmet
-- (test alias a19b = `s 19(2) the person is one of those who may make the declaration to the Registrar`)
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the person is one of those who may make the declaration to the Registrar` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) a registered qualified individual engaged in the formation of the proposed company"
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the person is one of those who may make the declaration to the Registrar` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) a person named in the constitution as a director or the secretary of the proposed company"
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the person is one of those who may make the declaration to the Registrar` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- anyone else: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a19c = `s 19(2) the declaration required by the subsection has been made to the Registrar`)
-- arguments: made by a person in (a) or (b); states (c) all requirements complied with; states (d) identities verified
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the declaration required by the subsection has been made to the Registrar` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(c) all of the requirements of this Act relating to the formation of the company have been complied with; and (d) he or she has verified the identities"
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the declaration required by the subsection has been made to the Registrar` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- made by someone outside (a) and (b)
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the declaration required by the subsection has been made to the Registrar` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c) not stated
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the declaration required by the subsection has been made to the Registrar` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (d) not stated
-- (test alias a19d = `s 19(2) the Registrar may accept the declaration as sufficient evidence of those matters`)
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the Registrar may accept the declaration as sufficient evidence of those matters` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the Registrar may accept such declaration as sufficient evidence of those matters"
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the Registrar may accept the declaration as sufficient evidence of those matters` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another declaration: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a19e = `s 19(3) the Registrar must register the company by registering its constitution`)
-- arguments: received the documents, information and payment of (1); received the declaration of (2); another provision of the Act (such as section 20) requires the Registrar not to register
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the Registrar must register the company by registering its constitution` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Upon receipt of the documents, information and payment referred to in subsection (1) and declaration mentioned in subsection (2), the Registrar must ... register the company"
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the Registrar must register the company by registering its constitution` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no documents, information and payment received: a duty whose "upon" gate is unmet (marginal reading (a))
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the Registrar must register the company by registering its constitution` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no declaration received: a duty whose "upon" gate is unmet
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the Registrar must register the company by registering its constitution` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "subject to this Act": another provision requires the Registrar not to register
-- (test alias a19f = `s 19(3) the document is the constitution of the company registered with the Registrar under section 19, as amended from time to time`)
-- arguments: the document is the constitution submitted under (1)(a), or that constitution as amended; the Registrar registered the company by registering that constitution
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the document is the constitution of the company registered with the Registrar under section 19, as amended from time to time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE   -- the seam: "the constitution of the company which is registered with the Registrar under section 19, as may be amended from time to time"
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the document is the constitution of the company registered with the Registrar under section 19, as amended from time to time` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE   -- not registered
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the document is the constitution of the company registered with the Registrar under section 19, as amended from time to time` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE   -- not the constitution submitted
-- (test alias a19g = `s 19(4) the Registrar must issue a notice of incorporation`)
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the Registrar must issue a notice of incorporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "On the registration of the constitution the Registrar must issue in the prescribed manner a notice of incorporation"
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the Registrar must issue a notice of incorporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not registered: a duty whose "on" gate is unmet (marginal reading (a))
-- (test alias a19h = `s 19(4) the notice of incorporation states what the subsection requires`)
-- arguments: issued in the prescribed manner and form; states the company is incorporated on and from a date; the kind of company the notice states; the kind the company is; the company is a private company; the notice states that it is a private company
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the notice of incorporation states what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE `limited by shares` `limited by shares` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) a company limited by shares", not a private company so nothing more to state
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the notice of incorporation states what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE `limited by guarantee` `limited by guarantee` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) a company limited by guarantee"
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the notice of incorporation states what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE `unlimited` `unlimited` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(c) an unlimited company"
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the notice of incorporation states what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE `limited by shares` `limited by shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "and where applicable, that it is a private company": stated
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the notice of incorporation states what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE `limited by shares` `limited by shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a private company, and the notice does not say so
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the notice of incorporation states what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE `limited by guarantee` `limited by shares` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "as the case may be": the notice states the wrong kind
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the notice of incorporation states what the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE `limited by shares` `limited by shares` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not in the prescribed manner or form
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the notice of incorporation states what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE `limited by shares` `limited by shares` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no date of incorporation stated
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the notice of incorporation states what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE `limited by shares` `limited by shares and by guarantee` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a company limited both by shares and by guarantee: not one of (a) to (c)
-- (test alias a19i = `s 19(5) the person is, with the other members, a body corporate capable of exercising all the functions of an incorporated company`)
-- arguments: a subscriber or another person who has become a member; the date asked; the date of incorporation in the notice; another provision of the Act provides otherwise
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is, with the other members, a body corporate capable of exercising all the functions of an incorporated company` TRUE (Date 5 1 2026) (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "On and from the date of incorporation specified in the notice": the day itself
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is, with the other members, a body corporate capable of exercising all the functions of an incorporated company` TRUE (Date 6 1 2026) (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- after that date
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is, with the other members, a body corporate capable of exercising all the functions of an incorporated company` TRUE (Date 4 1 2026) (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the day before: a failed "on and from" (periods ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is, with the other members, a body corporate capable of exercising all the functions of an incorporated company` TRUE (Date 6 1 2026) (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "but subject to this Act": the provision that overrides is outside this subsection
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is, with the other members, a body corporate capable of exercising all the functions of an incorporated company` FALSE (Date 6 1 2026) (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- anyone else: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a19j = `s 19(5) the liability of the members to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up`)
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the liability of the members to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up`  EQUALS NOTHING   -- "with such liability ... as is provided by this Act": the text points outside the subsection
-- (test alias a19k = `s 19(6) the subscriber is deemed to have agreed to become a member of the company`)
#ASSERT `s 19(6) the subscriber is deemed to have agreed to become a member of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "The subscribers to the constitution are deemed to have agreed to become members of the company"
#ASSERT `s 19(6) the subscriber is deemed to have agreed to become a member of the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- anyone else: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a19l = `s 19(6) the subscriber must be entered as a member in the register`)
-- arguments: the company has been incorporated; a public company; a private company; the register
#ASSERT `s 19(6) the subscriber must be entered as a member in the register` TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 19(6)(a) the register of members kept by the public company under section 190` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) in the case of a public company"
#ASSERT `s 19(6) the subscriber must be entered as a member in the register` TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 19(6)(b) the electronic register of members kept by the Registrar under section 196A` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) in the case of a private company"
#ASSERT `s 19(6) the subscriber must be entered as a member in the register` TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 19(6)(a) the register of members kept by the public company under section 190` EQUALS NOTHING   -- a private company and the public company's register: the text names no such entry
#ASSERT `s 19(6) the subscriber must be entered as a member in the register` TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 19(6)(b) the electronic register of members kept by the Registrar under section 196A` EQUALS NOTHING   -- a public company and the electronic register: the text names no such entry
#ASSERT `s 19(6) the subscriber must be entered as a member in the register` TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 19(6) another register` EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other register: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 19(6) the subscriber must be entered as a member in the register` FALSE TRUE FALSE `s 19(6)(a) the register of members kept by the public company under section 190` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not yet incorporated: a duty whose "on" gate is unmet (marginal reading (a))
-- (test alias a19m = `s 19(6A) the person is a member of the company`)
-- arguments: agrees to become a member; is a subscriber mentioned in (6); public company; private company; name entered in the register kept under section 190; name entered in the electronic register under section 196A
#ASSERT `s 19(6A) the person is a member of the company` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) in the case of a public company -- in the register of members kept by the public company under section 190"
#ASSERT `s 19(6A) the person is a member of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) in the case of a private company -- in the electronic register of members kept by the Registrar under section 196A"
#ASSERT `s 19(6A) the person is a member of the company` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a public company, entered only in the electronic register: the text does not say they are a member
#ASSERT `s 19(6A) the person is a member of the company` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a subscriber: (6A) speaks of "every other person"
#ASSERT `s 19(6A) the person is a member of the company` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- does not agree to become a member: the text does not say
-- (test alias a19n = `s 19(7) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation`)
#ASSERT `s 19(7) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Upon the application of a company and payment of the prescribed fee"
#ASSERT `s 19(7) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- fee unpaid: a duty whose "upon" gate is unmet (marginal reading (a))
#ASSERT `s 19(7) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application: a duty whose "upon" gate is unmet

§ `s 20: power to refuse registration`
-- (test alias a20a = `s 20(1) the Registrar must not register the constitution`)
-- arguments: a constitution is delivered for registration under section 19; the Registrar is satisfied that all the requirements have been complied with
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the Registrar must not register the constitution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the Registrar must not register the constitution unless the Registrar is satisfied that all the requirements of this Act ... have been complied with"
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the Registrar must not register the constitution` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the Registrar is satisfied": an "unless", met
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the Registrar must not register the constitution` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no constitution delivered for registration: a failed "where" (the bar does not arise)
-- (test alias a20b = `s 20(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the constitution of the proposed company`)
-- arguments: satisfied of (a) unlawful purpose or prejudicial purposes; satisfied of (b) contrary to national security or interest
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the constitution of the proposed company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) the proposed company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore"
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the constitution of the proposed company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) it would be contrary to the national security or interest for the proposed company to be registered"
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the constitution of the proposed company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither: a duty whose "where" gate is unmet (marginal reading (a))
-- (test alias a20c = `s 20(3) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision`)
-- arguments: aggrieved by the decision under subsection (2); the date of the decision; the date the appeal is brought
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "within 30 days of the date of the decision": 1 March plus 30 days is 31 March
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the day of the decision is in time (fork line F-H-P2)
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day late: a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before the decision: no appeal lies yet
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not aggrieved: "Any person aggrieved" (limited by its own wording)
-- (test alias a20d = `s 20(3) the decision of the Minister on the appeal is final`)
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the decision of the Minister on the appeal is final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the Minister whose decision is final"
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the decision of the Minister on the appeal is final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another decision: the text says nothing

§ `s 20A: minimum of one member`
-- (test alias a20e = `s 20A the company has at least one member`)
#ASSERT `s 20A the company has at least one member` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "A company must have at least one member": one
#ASSERT `s 20A the company has at least one member` 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- two
#ASSERT `s 20A the company has at least one member` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- none

§ `Regulative rules of ss 19 and 20: no time limit and no consequence the text states, so no breach path`
-- With no deadline, a late act still reads FULFILLED and no act reads RESIDUAL; the rules appear in "Rules with no breach path" in NOTES.md.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(1)(a) rule: the person desiring incorporation's duty to submit the constitution and documents` (Individual "Priya") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Priya" DOES `s 19(1)(a) submit to the Registrar the constitution of the proposed company and such other documents as may be prescribed` AT 900
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 19(1)(a) rule: the person desiring incorporation's duty to submit the constitution and documents` (Individual "Priya") AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(1)(b) rule: the person desiring incorporation's duty to furnish the last day of the first financial year` (Individual "Priya") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Priya" DOES `s 19(1)(b) furnish the Registrar with the last day of the proposed company's first financial year and such other information as may be prescribed` AT 900
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 19(1)(b) rule: the person desiring incorporation's duty to furnish the last day of the first financial year` (Individual "Priya") AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(1)(c) rule: the person desiring incorporation's duty to pay the prescribed fee` (Individual "Priya") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Priya" DOES `s 19(1)(c) pay the Registrar the prescribed fee` AT 900
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 19(1)(c) rule: the person desiring incorporation's duty to pay the prescribed fee` (Individual "Priya") AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(2) rule: the duty to make the declaration to the Registrar` (Individual "Priya") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Priya" DOES `s 19(2) make the declaration to the Registrar` AT 900
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 19(2) rule: the duty to make the declaration to the Registrar` (Individual "Priya") AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(3) rule: the Registrar's duty to register the company` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 19(3) register the company by registering its constitution` AT 900
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 19(3) rule: the Registrar's duty to register the company` 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(4) rule: the Registrar's duty to issue a notice of incorporation` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 19(4) issue a notice of incorporation` AT 900
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 19(4) rule: the Registrar's duty to issue a notice of incorporation` 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(7) rule: the Registrar's duty to issue the certificate of confirmation of incorporation` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 19(7) issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation` AT 900
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 19(7) rule: the Registrar's duty to issue the certificate of confirmation of incorporation` 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 20(2) rule: the Registrar's duty to refuse to register the constitution` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 20(2) refuse to register the constitution` AT 900
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 20(2) rule: the Registrar's duty to refuse to register the constitution` AT 0 WITH
-- s 20(1): a bar derived from "must not register ... unless ... satisfied".
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 20(1) rule: the Registrar's bar on registering the constitution` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 20(1) register the constitution` AT 4
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 20(1) rule: the Registrar's bar on registering the constitution` AT 0 WITH
